<title>USA: ValuJet says dangerous cargo was disguised.</title>
<headline>ValuJet says dangerous cargo was disguised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>ValuJet Airlines Inc. alleged on Thursday that maintenance company SabreTech Corp. deliberately disguised dangerous cargo suspected in the May 1996 crash of Flight 592 in the Florida Everglades.</p>
<p>ValuJet said it had asked the National Transportation Safety Board to investigate this &quot;new evidence&quot; before issuing a final conclusion about the cause of the crash, which killed all 110 people on board the DC-9.</p>
</text>
